pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The same slack overflow reached straight from the formula: both rows have a left-hand
% side in {0,2} and a hugely negative right-hand side, so both are trivially true and
% EVERY assignment is a model. Unfixed, the wrapped slack made row 1 assert x1 and row 2
% assert ~x1, so the trail was in conflict before the proof started and `rup >= 1 ;`
% derived the empty contradiction.
f 2 ;
rup >= 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
